Spec: ServiceReconfigureCmd

Purpose:
  Out of the build graph — this file is dead: ./mod.rs keeps `//mod reconfigure;`, the
    @Commands::Reconfigure variant and the exit-6 arm all commented (frozen in ./mod.sdd),
    so nothing here ever compiles, cargo never tests it, and it is unreachable from clap.
    Everything below is therefore the PROPOSAL frozen verbatim from the source, labelled
    as such, not live behaviour.
  If reconnected, back `agent service reconfigure`: resolve one @ServiceInstance by
    namespace and name, publish it as the process-wide owner context and as the Rhai
    variable `instance`, inject the parsed CLI flags as `args`, then hand off in order to
    the Rhai modules `context` and `reconfigure`. This file runs no reconfigure stage
    itself and writes no `status` — engine prep and handoff only.
  Diff-verified shape ancestor is ./install.rs: identical except the two instance-flag
    doc words (`install` → `reconfigure`), the `args` injection error channel
    (`@unwrap()` here, @map_err + `?` there) and the snippet's last import; the ten-flag
    block is verbatim identical. Cross-kind twin ./../tenant/reconfigure.rs differs only
    at the kind segment, owner setter and instance type — plus a formatting divergence
    recorded as a Task cross-ref.

Structure:
  ./reconfigure.rs: dead source, compiled only if ./mod.rs is uncommented per ./mod.sdd

References:
  ./install.sdd — shape ancestor; the flag, JSON-key and error-lane contracts mirror it
    verbatim except where `Purpose` names the diffs.
  ./mod.sdd — owns the freeze: the commented @Commands::Reconfigure variant and the exit-6
    error lane `Reconfiguring of a package failed with: {e:}` that would drive this file.
  ../tenant/reconfigure.rs — cross-kind twin (read-only comparison; its `{}` path
    interpolation without `@Path::display` never compiles, see Tasks).
  /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.rs — package entry-point pattern `reconfigure.rhai`;
    /docs/packages/lifecycle.md documents the reconfigure operation — the only live users
    of the name besides the commented lines in ./mod.rs.

Depends on:
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new resolver-directory semantics and registration
    set, @Script::set_dynamic, @Script::ctx, @Script::eval error lane.
  /common/src/instanceservice.sdd — @ServiceInstance and the @ServiceInstance::get lookup
    awaited here (attached by @impl_instance_common!).
  /common/src/context.sdd — @set_service store semantics and runtime preconditions.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Result, @common::Error variants, @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE
    as the `agent_image` clap default.
  @clap @Args, @serde, @serde_json — flag parsing and the derives behind the `args` JSON.
  ./mod.rs — the sole caller, commented: the awaited call and exit-6 `unwrap_or_else` lane.
  /agent/scripts/service/context.rhai — resolvable handoff script under the default
    `--script-dir`; no shipped `reconfigure.rhai` counterpart exists (see Handles).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap @Args struct deriving @Debug, @Serialize, @Deserialize; would mount on
    the commented @Commands::Reconfigure in ./mod.rs, so no live mount today; all ten fields
    module-private, reached only by the derives and @run.
  @run — @pub async fn @run(@args: @&@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>; the commented
    mod arm awaits this exact signature — async/await already agree, no mismatch to fix on
    revival.

Accepts:
  @Parameters.namespace — `-n` / `--namespace`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name `NAMESPACE`,
    @String, required.
  @Parameters.instance — `-i` / `--instance`, env `INSTANCE`, value name `INSTANCE`,
    @String, required; names the CR to fetch, never validated here.
  @Parameters.vynil_namespace — `-v` / `--vynil-namespace`, env `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, value
    name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, @String, required; reaches scripts only through `args`.
  @Parameters.package_dir — `-p` / `--package-dir`, env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `/tmp/package`.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/scripts`.
  @Parameters.template_dir — `-t` / `--template-dir`, env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/templates`; read by
    nothing in this Rust lane.
  @Parameters.agent_image — long-only `--agent-image`, env `AGENT_IMAGE`, value name
    `AGENT_IMAGE`, @String, clap default @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE, i.e.
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`.
  @Parameters.tag — long-only `--tag`, env `TAG`, value name `TAG`, @String, required,
    forwarded verbatim in `args`, never parsed or validated as a version here.
  @Parameters.config_dir — `-c` / `--config-dir`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name `CONFIG_DIR`,
    @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `.`.
  @Parameters.controller_values — long-only `--controller-values`, env `CONTROLLER_VALUES`,
    value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, @String, clap default the two-character string `{}`.
  Implicit runtime preconditions frozen as in ./install.sdd: a live tokio multi-thread
    runtime for @context::set_service, and @context::init_k8s already called by @service::run
    (inert either way).

Returns:
  @Ok(@()) once the fixed snippet completes without a Rhai error — the snippet's @Dynamic
    is discarded by `let _ =` and never inspected.

Raises:
  Frozen-if-recompiled error surface; nothing raises today because the file never runs.
  @common::Error::KubeError from the `?` on the awaited @ServiceInstance::get — missing
    @ServiceInstance (no default-to-absent), wrong namespace, Forbidden — the first fallible
    step, nothing published when it fails.
  @common::Error::Core (wrapping the Rhai error, Display `Rhai script error: <rhai text>`)
    from the `?` on @Script::eval: snippet parse error, missing `context` or `reconfigure`
    import, or a thrown error inside either module.
  @std::panic! from @serde_json::to_value(args) followed by `@unwrap()` — a serialization
    failure aborts by panic instead of yielding @common::Error::SerializationError the way
    ./install.rs does; unreachable in practice through the derives. The workspace denies
    product-code @unwrap, invisible to the harness only while this file stays out of the
    build graph (see Tasks and /linting.sdd).
  The context-owned @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` surfacing through
    @ServiceInstance::get → @get_client_async with no resolvable cluster configuration.
  @set_service panics on a current-thread or absent runtime (contract in
    /common/src/context.sdd), not catchable by the `?` lanes.

Handles:
  Every @Err lane belongs to the commented mod arm — frozen @tracing::error line
    `Reconfiguring of a package failed with:` then @process::exit(6) per ./mod.sdd; this
    file logs nothing and never exits.
  No shipped `reconfigure.rhai` anywhere in /agent/scripts — default revival therefore dies
    at the second import unless the mounted package supplies `scripts/reconfigure.rhai`,
    the first search directory; `context.rhai` resolves from `{script_dir}/service`.
  Eval failure after @set_service already ran — the process keeps the
    @VynilContext::ServiceInstance variant for the remaining process lifetime (it ends in
    the exit-6).
  Rerun over a configured instance — no `status` branch here: both modules replay; any
    idempotence is script-side.
  Flags with no local reader (`vynil_namespace`, `tag`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `controller_values`) — their only observable use is the `args` JSON the scripts consume.

Must:
  Execute in this order with nothing between: build the interpreter, fetch the CR, publish
    context, inject `instance`, serialize and inject `args`, evaluate the snippet, return
    @Ok — the @run skeleton of ./install.rs verbatim except the two diffs named in `Purpose`.
  Build the interpreter with @Script::new on exactly four resolver directories in this
    order: `{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}` (the bare directory), `{script_dir}/service`,
    `{script_dir}/lib` — plain interpolation of @std::path::Display via `@Path::display`,
    so a trailing `/` in a flag doubles the separator; earlier entries win an `import`.
  Fetch the CR with @ServiceInstance::get on clones of @Parameters.namespace and
    @Parameters.instance — one namespaced named read, never a list or create; an absent
    instance is an @Err, not a bootstrap path.
  Publish the fetched CR twice from the value and one clone: @set_service stores the clone
    as the process owner context and @rhai::Scope::set_value on @Script::ctx moves the
    original into the script variable named `instance`.
  Inject `args` as @Script::set_dynamic over @serde_json::to_value(args) — the object then
    carries exactly the ten snake_case keys `namespace`, `instance`, `vynil_namespace`,
    `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `tag`, `config_dir`,
    `controller_values` — @PathBuf values as path text, `agent_image` as a string,
    `controller_values` as a JSON string (its default renders `"{}"`, still a string).
  Evaluate the fixed four-statement snippet, nothing configurable in it, `context` first
    and `reconfigure` last:
      `import("context") as ctx;` `let context = ctx::run(instance, args);`
      `import("reconfigure") as reconfigure;` `reconfigure::run(instance, context);`
    — the map `ctx::run` returns becomes the second argument of `reconfigure::run`.
  Mutate nothing on the cluster itself: every write happens inside the Rhai modules through
    the registered @ServiceInstance bridge; no @ConditionsType names a reconfigure stage,
    and this lane reads the CR only.
  Emit no log and no stdout/stderr.

Must not:
  Branch on `status`, `tag` or `controller_values` in Rust: what reconfigure skips or
    replays is a script-side decision this lane never pre-empts.
  Render templates or apply manifests from Rust — `template_dir` steers no Rust code here,
    only the scripts through `args`.

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide revive vs delete: resurrect as a commented triplet in ./mod.rs
      (`//mod reconfigure;`, the @Commands::Reconfigure variant, the exit-6 arm) or delete
      this file; the decision is shared with the matching task in ./mod.sdd and must close
      in lockstep there.
  [ ] Untested: no test invokes @run — the file is never compiled, so none could; if
      revived, first cover every Scenario under the project TTD rule.
  [?] Twin formatting divergence: ../tenant/reconfigure.rs interpolates the @PathBuf fields
      with bare `{}` where this file calls `@Path::display` — @PathBuf does not implement
      @std::fmt::Display, so reconnected the tenant twin fails to compile while this copy
      would, and the tenant mod is commented out too (../tenant/mod.rs). Decide which copy
      is canonical before reviving either (read-only comparison recorded, nothing changed).
  [?] @unwrap vs @map_err: serialization failure panics here where ./install.rs returns
      @common::Error::SerializationError; reconnected, the deny on product-code @unwrap in
      /linting.sdd turns this line into a hard clippy failure. Decide to normalize onto the
      install lane (or keep the panic, contradicting the workspace rule).
  [?] No shipped `reconfigure.rhai`: /agent/scripts carries `context.rhai` but no reconfigure
      script for any kind, so revival is inert-with-an-import-error until either packages
      supply `scripts/reconfigure.rhai` (their entry-point pattern per
      /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.rs) or the agent ships one. Decide the supplier before
      the flag contract goes live.
  [?] Required-but-unread flags (`vynil_namespace`, `tag`) and the deserialization-less
      @Deserialize derive match ./install.rs exactly; if this file revives it inherits the
      open `[?]` set in ./install.sdd unchanged — resolve once there instead of duplicating.

Done when:
  The revive-or-delete decision is on record here and in ./mod.sdd; if revived, every
    Scenario has a passing test, clippy and fmt are green (which requires the @unwrap and
    twin-formatting divergences decided), and the shared flag questions closed.

Scenario: full run hands off in order with a package-supplied script
  Given all required flags supplied, an existing namespaced @ServiceInstance, and
    `reconfigure.rhai` shipped by the mounted package under its `scripts` directory (the
    only default location it can resolve from)
  When @run is awaited
  Then @Script::new received the four search dirs `[package]/scripts`, `[config]`,
    `[script]/service`, `[script]/lib` in that order
  And before the eval @set_service published the service variant and `instance` and `args`
    are bound
  Then `ctx::run(instance, args)` executes before `reconfigure::run(instance, context)`,
    and the map it returns is exactly the second argument `reconfigure::run` receives
  And @run returns @Ok(()) whatever the discarded @Dynamic was

Scenario: args JSON equals the install ten keys at defaults
  Given a command line setting only the required flags
  When @run serializes @Parameters into `args`
  Then the object holds exactly the ten keys `namespace`, `instance`, `vynil_namespace`,
    `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `tag`, `config_dir`,
    `controller_values`
  And `controller_values` is the JSON string `"{}"`, `template_dir` is `./agent/templates`
    and `agent_image` is `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`

Scenario: missing CR fails before any handoff
  Given no @ServiceInstance at that namespace/name — or its read is Forbidden
  When @run is awaited
  Then the `?` on @ServiceInstance::get returns @Err(@common::Error::KubeError)
  And @set_service never ran, neither injection happened and the snippet never evaluated,
    so the exit-6 lane would log `Reconfiguring of a package failed with:` carrying the
    KubeError text

Scenario: default script tree cannot satisfy the reconfigure import
  Given a valid @ServiceInstance, default `--script-dir` and a package directory holding no
    `reconfigure.rhai`
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then the `context` import succeeds and `reconfigure` import fails, @Script::eval returns
    @Err(@common::Error::Core Display-prefixed `Rhai script error:`)
  And the process context already holds the service variant when the exit-6 log fires
